'''''Lycium schweinfurthii''''' is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Solanaceae]]. The plant occurs in the south of the Mediterranean in Algeria, Tunisia, Libya, Egypt, Israel, Cyprus and southern Aegean (Crete, Karpathos, Rhodes) and Sicily and Pantelleria.<ref name="Feinbrun">Naomi Feinbrun: ''The genus Lycium in the Flora Orientalis region.'' In: ''Collectanea Botanica.'' Band 7, Nr. 1, 1968, S. 359--379 (''Lycium schweinfurthii'': S. 367--370), [http://bibdigital.rjb.csic.es/ing/RJB.php?Libro=2838&Desde=366&Hasta=386&Paginas= PDF-Datei].</ref>

